"PIP — YOUR WEEK
Mon 7 – Sun 13 Sep

3 THINGS WORTH A LOOK.

EVERYTHING, THIS MORNING
£11,430
Down £316 this week  ·  −2.7%

THE THREE POTS
Foundation   £8,240   Down £119 this week  ·  −1.4%
  On the 75% you set
  [|||||||||||||||||       ]
Handpicked   £2,410   Down £172 this week  ·  −6.7%
  On the 25% you set
  [|||||                   ]
Side Bet   £780   Down £25 this week  ·  −3.1%   [CAPPED]
  Money in is past 80% of its limit.
  [||                      ]

Foundation and Handpicked are judged against
the shape you set. Side Bet sits outside it,
with its own limit — in Setup, behind the
dots.

- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
[RECOMMENDATION]
PIP'S TAKE ON SIDE BET

THE FACT
Side Bet's value has grown past its limit —
10% of the net assets you gave Pip.

PIP'S TAKE
Take some profit — the part above the limit.

WHY
A punt that outgrows its limit stops being
small. The pounds are in Pip, where your net
assets stay behind the dots.

WHAT A DISCIPLINED INVESTOR USUALLY DOES
A disciplined investor usually takes some
profit when a punt outgrows its limit, so a
small bet stays small.

THE TRADE-OFF
If it keeps climbing, what you take out won't
climb with it. Outside an ISA, a sale can
count towards capital gains tax.

YOUR CALL.
Pip can't act on this, and there's no button
here on purpose. Moving money happens at your
broker.

See in Pip: https://pip.example.com/week

- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
[AWARENESS]
APPLE IS UP £50 THIS WEEK

That's 9.8%, past the 7% line you set for
Handpicked. Big moves happen; this is here so
it isn't a surprise.

Checks passed: Not on your exclusions list;
Past your big-move line; Side Bet has room
under its cap; Inside your weekly limit.
See in Pip: https://pip.example.com/week

- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
[AWARENESS]
ASML IN THE NEWS

Sample words from stub mode: Financial Times
and Reuters reported on ASML this week.

Sources: Financial Times; Reuters.
Checks passed: Side Bet has room under its
cap; Not on your exclusions list; Quiet around
